WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:29.040
We're down to just the last four days of this&nbsp;
campaign, but it may be more than four days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:36.080
until we know the final results in every state.
And that's OK. It's a modern thing that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.000
even expect to know the results on Election Day.&nbsp;
And this year, in particular, because there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.680
so many mail in ballots because of the global&nbsp;
100 year pandemic. Roughly 80 million people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.760
have already voted. And some states like&nbsp;
Pennsylvania, because they don't start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.400
counting those mail in votes until the polls close&nbsp;
on Tuesday, might not have results for a few days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:05.840
And that's okay. But it's not OK for Donald Trump,&nbsp;
because that is exactly the window of opportunity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.760
He is planning on to steal this election. Here&nbsp;
is Donald Trump. Don't take my word for it.&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.400
Here is Trump himself saying, hopefully&nbsp;
we will get courts to stop the counting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:25.040
of ballots that arrive after Election Day&nbsp;
or even just ballots that arrived on time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.840
but weren't counted before the end of&nbsp;
Election Day. Here's Trump himself saying it.&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.080
Hopefully a few states remaining that want to take&nbsp;
a lot of time after November 3rd to count ballots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.640
that won't be allowed by the various courts&nbsp;
because, as you know, we're in courts on that. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:47.280
just had a big victory yesterday in Wisconsin on&nbsp;
that matter. So hopefully that won't be happening.&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.880
OK, now, later on today, I'm going to talk&nbsp;
about how, of course, mail in ballots should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.080
be counted after Election Day as long&nbsp;
as they are postmarked by Election Day.&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.840
You have the as you have until Election Day itself&nbsp;
to vote, you shouldn't be penalized for delays in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.520
the mail. But the point here is that Donald Trump&nbsp;
is not trying to hide it. And when I've asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.440
Congresswoman Debbie McCaskill Powell about this,&nbsp;
I asked Mayor Eric Garcetti about this. I asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:22.240
Congressman Ruben Kago about this. Is Biden&nbsp;
ready with lawyers? They all say, yes, he is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.800
And that may well be true, but what if it gets to&nbsp;
the Supreme Court, which now has three of Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.200
Trump's nominated justices on it, and they get&nbsp;
to decide the outcome of these ballots in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:42.720
election? Donald Trump's plan is to block&nbsp;
legally cast ballots from counting. That is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:49.680
election fraud. That is voter suppression. That&nbsp;
is election suppression. It is against the law.&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:55.680
But they are trying to build public support&nbsp;
for stopping the counting of these ballots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.400
by pretending there would be something wrong&nbsp;
with counting them after Election Day. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.280
always the case, by the way, that this happens.&nbsp;
The only difference is that this time there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:11.040
more mail in ballots than ever because of the&nbsp;
pandemic. And Donald Trump, although now his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.400
postmaster general says he stopped Donald&nbsp;
Trump's postmaster general, was interfering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.840
with the post offices ability to handle mail.
So it might take a little bit longer. It might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.560
actually make a difference in a couple of states&nbsp;
that we don't get all of the ballots counted on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.000
election night. Now, some good news in terms&nbsp;
of rulings. The Supreme Court late Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.360
said both North Carolina and Pennsylvania will be&nbsp;
allowed to extend their arrival deadlines for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.840
mail in ballots. Again, we're not changing the&nbsp;
postmark date. You still have to fill it out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:48.640
mail it by Election Day. But they are extending&nbsp;
the transit deadline essentially. Increasingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.200
it really could be Pennsylvania. That is the&nbsp;
big one here. Pennsylvania could decide the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.040
winner. In fact, there's lots of electoral&nbsp;
votes, scenarios which we will go through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.520
where it comes down to Pennsylvania.
And secretary of pencils of the Commonwealth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:09.920
Pennsylvania, Kay Kathy Boockvar, said she expects&nbsp;
the overwhelming majority of votes will be counted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:16.000
by Friday, November 6th. It's just a few days,&nbsp;
but we could actually be waiting for Pennsylvania&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.640
depending on how the election goes. I would&nbsp;
prefer it not be that close, but it might be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:27.840
Eight states expect to have at least 98 percent of&nbsp;
unofficial results by noon Wednesday. Only eight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:35.840
22 states and D.C. allow postmarked ballots to&nbsp;
arrive after Election Day. So the timing is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:42.240
to depend on when voters return them. New York and&nbsp;
Alaska aren't going to report any mail in votes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.880
on election night. Shouldn't make a difference.&nbsp;
Alaska is going to Trump. New York is going very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:53.600
very powerfully to Joe Biden. Full results from&nbsp;
Michigan are expected to take several days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:05:00.160
If you combine now Pennsylvania and Michigan, you&nbsp;
really have many scenarios from an electoral map&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:06.400
standpoint where we don't know the results until&nbsp;
we know Michigan and Pennsylvania. If you say at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.200
this point, what are the odds networks will&nbsp;
announce a president elect on election night?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.320
I would say about 65 percent. Think there's&nbsp;
a 65 percent chance. It's it's not close. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.440
we know on election night, I think there's a 35&nbsp;
percent chance. We know at some point after that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.800
every vote must be counted. They are being&nbsp;
clear about their strategy. And I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:34.720
hope I know the members of Congress are telling&nbsp;
me Biden's got the lawyers ready. I hope he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.720
the right lawyers ready. I hope he has enough&nbsp;
lawyers ready because it's going to be a mess

